 calls that bypass the agent planner."},{"control_ids":["EXEC-02","SUP-05","OPS-02"],"how_it_helps":"Run the risky tool in a separate, disposable identity with no host mounts, ambient credentials, or unnecessary outbound access.","id":"execution-isolation","residual_limit":"Isolation limits reachable assets; it does not make injected code trustworthy or rule out a runtime escape.","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"}],"status":"proposed_not_verified","title":"Isolate tool execution","verification":"In a test environment, attempt reads outside the workspace, forbidden network connections, and resource exhaustion; retain policy and denial evidence."}],"finding_ids":["b1b0f0a3f33fe93875fcb58a"],"id":"group-45290f4fa5c7","image_context":"source","immediate_action":"Trace the input to eval/exec and replace it with fixed operations; if generated execution is essential, isolate it before accepting untrusted input.","locations":[{"end_line":16,"finding_id":"b1b0f0a3f33fe93875fcb58a","line":16,"path":"agent.py"}],"plausible_impact":"If external or generated content reaches this expression, it could execute Python with the process identity and access its files, credentials, and network.","priority":"P1","rule_id":"AI001","severity":"high","source_ids":["JOINT-DEPLOY","MCP-TOOLS","OWASP-AGENT-CS","OWASP-LLM2026","TECH-PYTHON-SECURITY"],"sources":[{"id":"JOINT-DEPLOY","title":"Deploying AI Systems Securely: Best Practices for Deploying Secure and Resilient AI Systems","url":"https://www.cyber.gov.au/business-government/secure-design/artificial-intelligence/deploying-ai-systems-securely"},{"id":"MCP-TOOLS","title":"MCP: Tools","url":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools"},{"id":"OWASP-AGENT-CS","title"